        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Per K. Sørensen, Frederick I of Saxony, William II of Meissen, Josef A. Käs, Jan Želivský\n- Organizations: Leipzig University\n- Roles: Tibetologist, Professor\n- Places: Saxony, Meissen\n- Topics: Tibetan and Himalayan history, literature, culture, Battle of Brüx\n\nFacts:\n- On December 2, 1409, Frederick I, Elector of Saxony, and his brother William II, Margrave of Meissen, founded Leipzig University with four scholastic faculties.\n- Frederick I of Saxony commanded the Catholic Imperial forces that defeated the Hussite troops led by Jan Želivský at the Battle of Brüx.\n- Per Kjeld Sørensen was born on 18 December 1950.\n- Per K. Sørensen is a prominent Danish Tibetologist who specializes in Tibetan and Himalayan history, literature, and culture.\n- Josef A. Käs is a Professor at Leipzig University.",
